FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied:
- Read the full parent grant list in fork_inner with named upper bounds (FORK_MAX_GRANTS, FORK_MAX_GRANT_SNAPSHOT_PASSES), repeating until two consecutive full reads match identically before mapping GRANT_SCHEME | GRANT_SHARED entries.
- Skip grant-fd EINVAL when a shared grant was unmapped after snapshot, keep EEXIST on mmap_remote as a real fork failure, and format grant-fd names on the stack without heap allocation.
- Arm ChildCleanupGuard after new_child_process in fork_inner (disarmed only after start succeeds) to terminate and reap any half-created child via ProcCall::Exit and bounded WNOHANG polling.

